[board-minutes-weekly] FIRST: self-rearm — read {{HOME}}/Documents/workbench/.claude/scheduled_tasks.json (project-scoped); find the task whose prompt starts with "[board-minutes-weekly]"; if createdAt is older than 5 days, CronDelete it and CronCreate an identical one (cron 27 6 * * 1, durable, recurring, same prompt) so the 7-day auto-expiry never lapses.
THEN: (1) render the week's minutes: cd ~/Documents/workato-kb && .venv/bin/python -m kb.board_minutes — it writes knowledge/dreams/board-minutes-<today>.md and reports sanitizer findings; if it says nothing to publish, relay that in one line and skip to the heartbeat.
(2) Publish as a DRAFT Confluence page via the atlassian MCP: cloudId workato.atlassian.net, spaceId 105054224 ([External] BT), parentId 2938830860, title "Board Minutes — Dreaming Team — <today YYYY-MM-DD>", contentFormat=markdown, body = the minutes file content, status=draft. DRAFT is mandatory (Josh publishes on review; new pages are Josh-gated).
(3) Read the page back and confirm the draft exists with formatting intact; report the draft URL + sanitizer finding count in 2 lines.
LAST STEP (never skip): heartbeat check-in: echo '{"ts":"<now ISO>","job":"board-minutes"}' | python3 ~/.claude/knowledge/scripts/atomic_io.py ~/.claude/knowledge/garden-reports/heartbeat.jsonl (atomic writer; NEVER a plain >> append — plain appends get wiped by concurrent atomic replaces)
